1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,122
The Great Pyramid was the tallest thing
people built for 3,800 years,

2
00:00:05,122 --> 00:00:08,279
and we thought nobody had written down how
they did it,

3
00:00:08,279 --> 00:00:12,182
until archaeologists found the diary of a
man who hauled its stones.

4
00:00:12,632 --> 00:00:18,156
His name was Merer, and his crew moved
just a few of its 2.3 million blocks,

5
00:00:18,156 --> 00:00:22,298
which went up its ramps at about one every
few minutes, every day,

6
00:00:22,298 --> 00:00:23,742
for about twenty years.

7
00:00:24,192 --> 00:00:27,892
Most were cut right beside it and dragged
on wooden sledges,

8
00:00:27,892 --> 00:00:30,851
while someone poured water on the sand in
front,

9
00:00:30,851 --> 00:00:34,304
because damp sand stays firm and the pull
drops by half.

10
00:00:34,754 --> 00:00:38,053
But the white outer stones came from
across the Nile,

11
00:00:38,053 --> 00:00:40,978
so Merer's forty men sailed them over in
boats,

12
00:00:40,978 --> 00:00:43,405
along canals dug almost to the pyramid.

13
00:00:43,855 --> 00:00:48,390
And they were cut so precisely that some
joints are thinner than a credit card,

14
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:52,465
so the pyramid shone white, until people
took them away to build Cairo.

15
00:00:52,915 --> 00:00:54,560
And its builders weren't slaves,

16
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:58,518
because they were paid in bread and beer
and buried right next to their king.

17
00:00:58,968 --> 00:01:03,144
So it wasn't aliens that built it, but
thousands of people like Merer,

18
00:01:03,144 --> 00:01:04,993
with ropes, boats and wet sand.
